---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/ui/Container.astro";
import Button from "@/components/ui/Button.astro";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: "Daniel Glazebrook",
  jobTitle: "Founder, Worm Studio",
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Worm Studio" },
  url: "https://wormstudio.co.uk/daniel-glazebrook",
  sameAs: "https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-james-glazebrook"
};
---

<Layout
  title="Daniel Glazebrook"
  description="About Worm Studio's founder, Daniel Glazebrook, and his background in SEO and web development."
  path="/daniel-glazebrook"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />

  <Container grid class="pt-20 pb-24">
    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wide">Words from our founder</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-ink leading-tight mt-3">
        Worm Studio is a new agency, but its expertise behind it aren't.
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 mt-8">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted">
        Worm Studio is new. I'm not. I've been working in SEO and digital marketing since 2012,
        and the creative industries for longer than that. Worm is the first
        time I've put both under one name, and I hope that you are as excited for the journey as I am.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        I've watched search change more in the last two years than in the previous
        decade. Google went from aiming to get ranked in the ten blue links to now being cited and named in AI Overviews.
        People stopped typing keywords into a search box and have started asking
        ChatGPT real questions instead. Most of what I learned about
        ranking a page in 2012 still matters - structure, clarity, actually
        answering the question in the clearest most authentic way - but the destination changed, and a lot of
        businesses haven't caught up yet.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-gold pl-4 mt-6 text-ink font-display text-xl italic">
        "Worm Studio is my first SEO agency, but it's not my first
        SEO project."
      </blockquote>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        I studied graphic design at the University of Brighton, then spent
        nine years as a full-stack web developer - mostly working at small design
        agencies, the kind where there's no separation in roles for the team. 
        The creative problem, and the creative solution are all one.
        The kind of environment where you end up doing a bit of everything: design, dev, content, marketing
        client calls, and then the SEO that makes the site actually worth
        building in the first place. SEO was the constant throughout all of
        my career - the part I kept coming back to, and the part I never stopped
        being passionate about.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        That hands-on, involved-in-everything approach is the actual
        foundation <a href="/#approach" class="text-ink underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-gold-deep">Worm Studio's approach</a> is built on - not a pivot into something
        new, just the same way of working, applied to where search is now.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        It's also why the first thing I did with this studio was check to check where we ranked as a new agency - unsurprisingly we didn't show in any Google search results or AI prompt answers. So I thought i'd document honestly our process of becoming a ranking SEO agency rather than just claim
        expertise - <a href="/blog/starting-from-zero-ai-search-baseline" class="text-ink underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-gold-deep">Starting from zero: does ChatGPT know Worm Studio exists?</a>.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <Button href="/#work" variant="outline">See how we work</Button>
        <Button href="/#approach" variant="text">Read our approach</Button>
        <Button href="/blog/starting-from-zero-ai-search-baseline" variant="text">Read the first case study</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>